From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Detect LuneOS from PalmSystem when the user agent does not say so

LuneOS.js gates every one of its event hooks on

    if (webOS.platform.legacy || webOS.platform.open || webOS.platform.luneos)

and sets platform.luneos only when the user agent contains "luneos". On a current
LuneOS build none of those three is ever set, so the whole block is skipped: no
Mojo.relaunch, no stageActivated/stageDeactivated, and - the one users notice -
no keyup -> `backgesture` emulation, which leaves an Enyo app with no back
gesture at all. On a phone layout that means a conversation, or any pushed view,
has no way back.

Two independent causes, both measured on a MindPhone (LuneOS, WAM with the
Chromium 151 webruntime):

1. The user agent no longer carries the marker:

     Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux armv7l) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko)
     Chrome/151.0.7922.108 Safari/537.36 WebAppManager

2. webOS.js (enyo-webos) never sets legacy or open either, because it decides
   between them with

     if (d.platformVersionMajor && d.platformVersionMinor)

   which is a truthiness test on a number that is legitimately zero. LuneOS
   reports platformVersion "3.0.5", so platformVersionMinor is 0, the branch is
   skipped, and no flag is set. Nothing throws, so the catch that would have set
   `open` does not run. Confirmed in the running app: major 3, minor 0, the
   shipped test false, a presence test true. That one wants fixing in webOS.js
   with a presence test; this patch does not depend on it.

So webOS.platform comes back as {} and the guard cannot pass. Fall back to
window.PalmSystem, which is the honest test for running inside a webOS app
container, and only when nothing else matched - so a TV, watch, legacy or Open
webOS build keeps whatever webOS.js decided.

Also fix the adjacent `webOS.plaform` typo, which meant that line guarded nothing
and would throw on the next line if webOS.js really were missing.

Verified on a MindPhone with this patch alone, the application-side workaround
disabled: webOS.platform.luneos is true, a keyup of keyCode 27 raises
`backgesture`, and in Messaging a conversation open at composer left=87 in a
480px viewport slides to left=567 - thread list showing - on that keyup. The
compositor really does send the key; CardView.onSwipeLeftGesture does
seat.sendKeyEvent(Qt.Key_Escape, true/false), and a capture-phase recorder caught
`keyup keyCode=27 key=Escape` arriving with no backgesture following it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted to JayCanuck/enyo-luneos]
---
--- a/LuneOS/LuneOS.js
+++ b/LuneOS/LuneOS.js
@@ -15,7 +15,9 @@
 		console.warn('WARNING: webOS.js missing. Will attempt to continue.');
 		window.webOS = {};
 	}
-	webOS.plaform = webOS.plaform || {};
+	// Was `webOS.plaform` - a typo, so this guarded nothing and the real object was whatever
+	// webOS.js left behind. Harmless until webOS.js is missing, when the lines below throw.
+	webOS.platform = webOS.platform || {};
 
 	// Mojo js hook system init
 	window.Mojo = window.Mojo || {};
@@ -25,6 +27,34 @@
 		webOS.platform.luneos = true;
 	}
 
+	// Fall back to PalmSystem when the user agent does not say "luneos" and webOS.js detected
+	// nothing either, which is the normal case on a current LuneOS build and leaves every
+	// platform-gated feature in this library switched off - including the keyup -> `backgesture`
+	// emulation below, so an app has no back gesture at all.
+	//
+	// Two independent reasons it ends up empty:
+	//
+	//  1. WAM's user agent no longer carries the marker. Measured on a MindPhone:
+	//     "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux armv7l) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko)
+	//      Chrome/151.0.7922.108 Safari/537.36 WebAppManager"
+	//
+	//  2. webOS.js decides legacy-vs-open with
+	//         if (d.platformVersionMajor && d.platformVersionMinor)
+	//     which is a truthiness test on a number that is legitimately zero. LuneOS reports
+	//     platformVersion "3.0.5", so platformVersionMinor is 0, the branch is skipped, and
+	//     neither platform.legacy nor platform.open is set. No exception is raised, so the
+	//     catch that would have set `open` never runs either. (The proper fix for that one is
+	//     a presence test in webOS.js; this fallback does not depend on it.)
+	//
+	// PalmSystem is the honest test for "running inside a webOS app container", and this only
+	// fires when nothing else matched, so a TV, watch, legacy or Open webOS build keeps the
+	// platform webOS.js gave it.
+	if(!webOS.platform.luneos && !webOS.platform.legacy && !webOS.platform.open &&
+			!webOS.platform.tv && !webOS.platform.watch && window.PalmSystem) {
+		webOS.platform.luneos = true;
+		delete webOS.platform.unknown;
+	}
+
 })();
 
 
